<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="3a840621">&lt;p&gt;
    Capturing requirement attributes can be an iterative process.  Revisit each requirement regularly throughout the
    development lifecycle to update or populate missing attributes.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="341712ea"></attribute>
<attribute name="usageGuidance" nodeId="7aeba47b"></attribute>
<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="ffcff6dc">&lt;p&gt;
    Attributes contain information about requirements to help obtain clarity. When captured properly, they can provide
    insight on the overall state of a system. The right level of attributes to capture will be determined in conjunction
    with the client. The overall goal is to get to the right level of detail so there is sufficient information without
    unnecessary detail.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Attributes can be pre-defined up front of they can be free form text (e.g., priority would be pre-defined to high,
    medium or low and requirement description would be free form text).&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
